Boken om Teknisk analys ar en pedagogisk skriven och lattlast grundbok som inte kraver nagra storre forkunskaper i amnet. Boken lar ut hur man optimerar tidpunkten for kop och forsaljning pa borsen. Metoden kompletterar den traditionella bors- och foretagsanalysen.
Den presenterar metoderna, variablerna och verktygen som utgor grundstenarna i den tekniska analysen och ar rikt illustrerad med exempel fran Stockholmsborsen.
Nagra av de fragestallningar och metoder som boken behandlar:
- Diagramteknik
- Signaler, trendlinjer, motstand och gaps
- Omslags- och fortsattningsformationer
- Trend-, volym- och momentumindikatorer
- Cykelanalys och Elliotts vagteori
Om forfattarna
Johnny Torssell ar teknisk analyschef pa BorsInsikt AB. Han har under mer an 15 ar studerat och arbetat med praktisk analys som tradingverktyg. Han har aven arbetat med fundamental aktieanalys, och ar skaparen bakom nr11-strategin. En strategi som tillampas for OMX-terminer.
Peter Nilsson ar verksam som teknisk och fundamental aktieanalytiker. Han har studerat teknisk analys under manga ar. Han ar Ekon.mag med inriktning pa finansiering i foretagsekonomi och har en Fil.kand i nationalekonomi.
Forfattarna blev hosten 1999 utnamnda till Arets tekniska analytiker av STAF, Sveriges Tekniska Analytikers Forening. De har aven tillsammans skrivit Boken om Trading och TNInfoStrategi samt Tradinghandboken."ñ
îGive and Take highlights what effective networking, collaboration, influence, negotiation, and leadership skills have in common.
For generations, we have focused on the individual drivers of success: passion, hard work, talent, and luck. But today, success is increasingly dependent on how we interact with others. It turns out that at work, most people operate as either takers, matchers, or givers. Whereas takers strive to get as much as possible from others and matchers aim to trade evenly, givers are the rare breed of people who contribute to others without expecting anything in return.
Using his own pioneering research as Wharton's youngest tenured professor, Grant shows that these styles have a surprising impact on success. Although some givers get exploited and burn out, the rest achieve extraordinary results across a wide range of industries. Combining cutting-edge evidence with captivating stories, this landmark book shows how one of America's best networkers developed his connections, why the creative genius behind one of the most popular shows in television history toiled for years in anonymity, how a basketball executive responsible for multiple draft busts transformed his franchise into a winner, and how we could have anticipated Enron's demise four years before the company collapsed - without ever looking at a single number.
Praised by bestselling authors such as Dan Pink, Tony Hsieh, Dan Ariely, Susan Cain, Dan Gilbert, Gretchen Rubin, Bob Sutton, David Allen, Robert Cialdini, and Seth Godin-as well as senior leaders from Google, McKinsey, Merck, Estee Lauder, Nike, and NASA - Give and Take highlights what effective networking, collaboration, influence, negotiation, and leadership skills have in common. This landmark book opens up an approach to success that has the power to transform not just individuals and groups, but entire organizations and communities."␀␀`@"	…ëQ¸@"	)\Âõ(@"	=
